      "Language": "rus",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "The article discusses a clinical case of combined surgical treatment for painful bullous keratopathy in an eye with uncompensated far-advanced glaucoma. Ex-PRESS Glaucoma Filtration Device was used for anterior chamber drainage. The procedure was supplemented by amniotic membrane implantation under the scleral flap, microdiathermocoagulation of large corneal epithelial bullae, and epikeratoplasty."},
